From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Will Faust <willtechnoduck@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 14:35:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ios: #52 pool-alias RIP redirect + ExitToX64 FFS bypass +
 callret predictor disable
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three verified fixes plus the probe infrastructure that found them:

1. CompileBlock (Core.cpp): a guest RIP inside a module's JIT-pool copy is
   reverse-translated via IosJitReverseTranslate and re-entered through the
   dispatcher loop-top (return Frame->Pointers.DispatcherLoopTop). The EC code
   bitmap only covers PE-space VAs, so pool-alias branch targets classified as
   x86 and the frontend decoded native ARM64 as x86 (ml314: PSAPI DllMain,
   ml299: ntdll+0x7488c x3422). ml315: 21 redirects, 0 'Invalid instruction in
   entry block', c000001d gone. Alias table is the discriminator — never a
   band test (guest images map in-band, ml198).

2. ExitToX64 (Module.S): detect the 14-byte x64 fast-forward sequence, reverse-
   translate the jmp target through IosAliasEntries, and if it is EC code per
   the bitmap, branch natively — preserving the x4/x5 varargs descriptor that
   the emulation round trip destroys. Dormant for the SCM path (which enters
   via the delay-load aux slot, fixed in wine) but correct hardening with
   taken/rejected counters so silence is meaningful.

3. BranchOps: callret predictor shortcut disabled on iOS (stack balance kept,
   stale-entry trust dropped) — correlated with the deepest runs of the
   session; Thumper cost ~250avg/350peak vs 200-300/450 (accepted).

Probes: [pool-rip-fix], [ffs-bypass], [cb-entry], [disp-addrs], dispatcher
witness fields (IosLastEnterECRip/Callback), MYTHIC_REV build stamp.

Madeira-commit: 49a7b55ec0b1a175782ba7fb4292f688412cffb4
Rebased: resolved
Class: madeira-port
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-09-24-fex-latest-rebase.md
Offered-upstream: no
